posts.body:
Save the following code as a plugin:
JavaScript:
// Plugin by Toby Yasha. No credits required, but appreciated.

Game_Unit.prototype.defense = function() {
    const members = this.members();
    const sum = members.reduce((r, member) => r + member.def, 0);
    return Math.max(1, sum / Math.max(1, members.length));
};

BattleManager.makeEscapeRatio = function() {
    this._escapeRatio = (0.5 * $gameParty.defense()) / $gameTroop.defense();
};

Yes it does matter. Now i don't know if their code also affects the escape rate, but if you want to ensure compatibility with their plugins, you should place the plugin i made anywhere below Visustella's battle plugins.
If you want to test if the plugin works or not you could set the escape rate to 1 and test it by escaping from 2-3 battles.
Here's how you would do it:
JavaScript:
BattleManager.makeEscapeRatio = function() {
    this._escapeRatio = 1;
};
After you are done with the test make sure to revert the formula back to the one i posted before.

